{"id": "DfCf7rPowtL", "title": "Video by therishikatha", "description": "Diwali is 5 days. Did you know Yamraj, the god of death, gets 3 of them? 🪔 Here’s what the Padma Purana says.\n\nDay 1, Dhanteras: one lamp goes OUTSIDE the door, for Yama. The Padma Purana says that by this, untimely death is avoided. Families turn it to face south, Yama’s direction.\n\nDay 2, Naraka Chaturdashi: a morning bath, then water offered to Yama by his 14 names: Yama, Dharmaraja, Mrityu, Antaka, Vaivasvata, Kala, Sarvabhutakshaya, Audumbara, Dadhna, Nila, Parameshthi, Vrikodara, Chitra, Chitragupta.\n\nDay 3, Amavasya: Lakshmi’s night.\nDay 4: Govardhan.\n\nDay 5, Bhai Dooj: long ago on this day, Yamuna fed her brother Yama in her own home. So on this day brothers eat from their sister’s hand.\n\nTwo days we keep Death away. On the third, even Death goes home to his sister. 🙏\n\n(Source: Padma Purana, Uttara Khanda, chapter 122, “The Celebration of Dipavali”.)\n\nWant your kids to grow up knowing our gods and their stories? Our picture books, Books 1–3, are a set of 3 for ₹500 👉 rishikatha.com (link in bio)\n\n💬 Does YOUR family light the Yama diya on Dhanteras? Comment YES or NO!\n🔁 Share this with your brother or sister before Bhai Dooj, and save it for Dhanteras.\n\n#diwali #dhanteras #yamadeepam #yamraj #bhaidooj narakachaturdashi chotidiwali diwali2026 padmapurana hindutraditions sanatandharma hindufestival yamuna rishikatha", "channel": "therishikatha", "uploader_id": "22569163881", "uploader": "Rishi Katha", "timestamp": 1793192789, "like_count": 14638, "comment_count": 36, "http_headers": {"Referer": "https://www.instagram.com/"}, "formats": [{"format_id": "dash-2346524639511656a", "ext": "m4a", "tbr": 60.072, "asr": 44100, "format_note": "DASH audio", "container": "m4a_dash", "vcodec": "none", "acodec": "mp4a.40.5", "url": "https://instagram.fblr22-1.fna.fbcdn.net/o1/v/t2/f2/m78/AQMQL5Bl9iEsSybi7OrBFsaB9Kb-QF3tgPCYcJf9UnKXKFSPi_WRmevmUqtu1_gcFrLdKGbG2FXFS6bn0zcmv89-DK7afdViq